{"created": "2026-09-25T20:14:45.709918+00:00", "modified": "2026-10-06T02:01:36.229408+00:00", "id": 22967456, "conceptrecid": "22967455", "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.22967456", "conceptdoi": "10.5281/zenodo.22967455", "doi_url": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.22967456", "metadata": {"title": "Two Transit-like Signals in TESS Photometry of the Nearby K Dwarf TIC 4206066", "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.22967456", "publication_date": "2026-09-25", "description": "<p>Preprint of a Research Note prepared for submission to the Research Notes of the AAS. Abstract: I report two transit-like signals in TESS photometry of the late-K dwarf TIC 4206066 (StKM 1-561), found in Sector 98 and traced back to Sectors 6 and 32. The 3.18 d signal (23 transits, ~500 ppm) corresponds to a 1.4 +/- 0.1 Earth-radius planet if it orbits the target. Vetting, localization, and Gaia astrometry, photometry, and radial velocities leave a planet transiting an unresolved bound companion as the main alternative host scenario; TRICERATOPS gives FPP = 0.03-0.04, mostly from companions these data disfavor. The lower-significance 11.13 d signal (~2.2 Earth radii if on the target; ~3 sigma in a post hoc test) is reported with a tentative ephemeris. No statistical validation is claimed. Supporting data and code: doi:10.5281/zenodo.22967099.</p>", "access_right": "open", "creators": [{"name": "Rabtsevich, Pavel", "affiliation": "Independent Researcher", "orcid": "0009-0005-0654-6658"}], "keywords": ["TESS", "TIC 4206066", "exoplanet candidates", "transit photometry"], "related_identifiers": [{"identifier": "10.5281/zenodo.22967099", "relation": "isSupplementedBy", "resource_type": "dataset", "scheme": "doi"}], "resource_type": {"title": "Preprint", "type": "publication", "subtype": "preprint"}, "license": {"id": "cc-by-4.0"}, "relations": {"version": [{"index": 0, "is_last": true, "parent": {"pid_type": "recid", "pid_value": "22967455"}}]}}, "title": "Two Transit-like Signals in TESS Photometry of the Nearby K Dwar